{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791692618,"nonce":"w0dtomtB/HqOmePTrlMgWrHH8W8=","message":"Decision: after rebasing onto C6 (PR 100) the lock order is run lock, console lock, migrate lock (innermost). Console start migrates under its shared console lock; db restore holds run + console exclusive and now also takes the migrate lock innermost (bounded 120s, refuses with nothing written on timeout) around its write of the live DB. Restore keeps its own schema guard on the staged copy and never calls migrate(). Reason: the console lock is always taken non-blocking and a migrate-lock holder never waits for another lock, so no cycle can form; taking it in restore stops a restore from writing mid-migration of a CLI command that holds no run lock.","files":null}]}